        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Verify signed marketplace feed refresh",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Wire signed marketplace feed profiles into hosted catalog refresh using the signed envelope verifier and configured threshold.\n- Persist bounded signed-feed trust state with hosted snapshots, and re-verify signed snapshots with the current source profile before using them.\n- Count signed-feed thresholds over unique normalized Ed25519 public-key material so duplicate key IDs or duplicate key material cannot weaken a multi-signature threshold.\n- Keep signed profiles fail-closed on invalid live bodies or unsigned old snapshots, without changing install eligibility or the existing marketplace refresh/entries payload shape.\n\n## Validation\n\n```text\n> node scripts\\run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  59 passed (59)\n\n> node node_modules\\oxlint\\bin\\oxlint --deny-warnings src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts\nPASS\n\n> node node_modules\\oxfmt\\bin\\oxfmt --check --threads=1 --config .oxfmtrc.jsonc src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.ts src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n\n> git diff --check\nPASS\n```\n## Real behavior proof\n\nCurrent head `5b9b2a5954` keeps the existing signed-refresh proof and adds regressions for the two requested trust-boundary fixes.\n\nThe focused catalog test lane now proves:\n\n```text\n> node scripts\\run-vitest.mjs src/plugins/official-external-plugin-catalog.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests  59 passed (59)\n```\n\nCoverage added in this head:\n\n- A signed feed profile loads and persists a verified sequence 10 snapshot, then rejects a validly signed sequence 9 refresh before returning or writing it; the loader falls back to the existing sequence 10 signed snapshot and `snapshotStore.write` is not called for the rollback.\n- A request that supplies both `feedProfile: \"acme\"` and a direct allowed `feedUrl` preserves the selected signed profile verification policy, so unsigned JSON from the URL override fails closed with `signed envelope is malformed` instead of being accepted as trusted hosted data.\n\nExisting branch proof still covers signed envelope acceptance, trust-state persistence, signed snapshot re-verification, and unsigned old snapshot rejection.\n## Stack notes\n\nThis is OpenClaw trust series PR #4 / OpenClaw PR #3, stacked after:\n\n- #98299 signed hosted feed envelope verifier primitives\n- #98316 source-profile trust config at `16cbe678ce`\n\nThe PR currently targets `main` as a draft because the dependency branches are on the fork. Reviewers should focus on the top commit `5b9b2a5954` until the earlier trust PRs land.\r\n",
